          "secret": "GEZDGNBVGY3TQOJQGEZDGNBVGY3TQOJQ",
          "algorithm": "SHA1",
          "digits": 6,
          "counter": 5
        },
        "969429",
        0,
        5
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "TOTP/HOTP.validate",
      "goFn": "otpauth.Key.Verify",
      "note": "a code for an ALREADY CONSUMED counter",
      "acceptance": true,
      "deviation": "upstream's HOTP window is symmetric, so a code for an ALREADY CONSUMED counter (delta -2) is accepted; the port's HOTP window is forward-only, which is what makes a consumed counter unreplayable. RFC 4226 section 7.4 requires the server to move the counter forward on a successful check. Deliberately not copied"
    },
